@* Pagination's Overview, written by hand after the selection Overviews: pages in the address, more
   than one on a page (code), sizes and how many pages show, and bound to C#. Accessibility and See
   also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>Pagination shows links to the pages of a long list. Each page is a link that sets <Code>?page=</Code> and keeps the rest of the URL, so paging works on static pages with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>, survives a reload, and can be shared.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Pagination only renders the links: your page reads the number and shows its own rows. A <Anchor Href="docs/components/table">Table</Anchor> pages itself with the same links.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Pages in the URL</Heading>
<TextBlock>To set how many pages there are, set <Code>TotalItems</Code> and <Code>PageSize</Code>, or <Code>PageCount</Code>. To show the page's rows, read the page number with <Code>[SupplyParameterFromQuery]</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="pagination-url" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>Page 1 leaves the key out of the URL.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Pagination treats a number past the last page as the last page. Clamp the number you read the same way.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On the first and last pages, Previous or Next stays in place, marked unavailable.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">More than one on a page</Heading>
<TextBlock>Two paginations on one page would share the <Code>page</Code> key. To give each its own key in the URL, so they page separately, set <Code>QueryKey</Code>. To name each one for screen readers, set <Code>Label</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Several</Code>
<TextBlock>When its filters change, a <Anchor Href="docs/components/filter-form">FilterForm</Anchor> removes a <Code>page</Code> key, or one ending in <Code>-page</Code>, from the URL, so filtering starts again at page 1.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and how many pages show</Heading>
<TextBlock>To match the buttons and fields around it, set <Code>Size</Code>. To set how many pages show on each side of the current one, set <Code>Siblings</Code>. To set how many pages always show at each end, set <Code>Boundaries</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="pagination-sizes" />
<TextBlock>The row keeps the same number of slots as the page changes, so the controls don't jump about. Below 640px, only the current page and the ends show, with a gap for each run left out, so the row fits a phone.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Binding the page</Heading>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, Pagination can page in C# instead of the URL. Bind the page with <Code>@@bind-Page</Code>. The pages become buttons that update the bound value, and the URL stays as it is.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="pagination-bound" />
<TextBlock>Static pages have no C# to update, so there the pages stay links that set the key. Start the bound value from the URL, so both render modes work. This example reads it from <Code>?p=</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>Pagination's text for screen readers can be renamed or translated. The navigation landmark's name is <Code>Label</Code>, "Pagination" by default. The arrows' names are <Code>PreviousLabel</Code> and <Code>NextLabel</Code>, "Previous page" and "Next page". The word read before each number is <Code>PageLabel</Code>, "Page".</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @foreach (var order in Orders.Skip((Page - 1) * 20).Take(20))
        {
            <OrderRow Order="order" />
        }
        <Pagination TotalItems="Orders.Count" PageSize="20" Label="Orders pages" />

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "page")]
            private int? CurrentPage { get; set; }

            private int PageCount => Math.Max(1, (Orders.Count + 19) / 20);
            private int Page => Math.Clamp(CurrentPage ?? 1, 1, PageCount);
        }
        """;

    private const string Several = """
        <Pagination TotalItems="Orders.Count" QueryKey="orders-page" Label="Orders pages" />
        <Pagination TotalItems="Returns.Count" QueryKey="returns-page" Label="Returns pages" />
        """;
}
